--- body ---
## Context
Follow-ups from ticket 1235 (PR #1704, merged 2026-10-27 on author override
after five gaze rounds). Items 1-2 are the author's design questions, answered
in session; items 3-10 are review findings the author deferred here.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] 1. Plan has a surprise rule: ask before executing (escalation protocol, advisor first) when the route departs from what the ticket's author would expect: another deliverable kind, work beyond **Relevant files**, a dropped or reinterpreted exit criterion, anything irreversible or outward-facing. Otherwise announce and proceed.
- [ ] 2. Plan checks for in-flight overlap: open merge requests and locked worktrees touching **Relevant files**; on overlap, name it in the plan and coordinate (PR comment, or a session message where the runtime allows); three or more on one file: a coordination change first (`rules/workflow.md`). Decide whether a helper script earns its place.
- [ ] 3. A ticket returned as a monster mid-Execute: say what becomes of its locked worktree and partial branch, and what raid does when no later wave is left.
- [ ] 4. `rules/workflow.md` monster line gives a lone autonomous session (neither orchestrator nor hunt) an action; stay inside the resident budget.
- [ ] 5. Simplify hunt: drop the third restatement of the monster return in Execute, drop the Detach final-report clause if redundant, shorten "Too big or multipart" to a pointer to `rules/workflow.md`.
- [ ] 6. Hunt's no-forge close stages narrowly, as `/merge` step Close does (`git add -u tickets/ && git add tickets/closed/<id>-*.erg`), not `tickets/` wholesale.
- [x] 7. Moved to ticket 1252 (author 2026-10-27: raid, hunt, gaze and merge must need no forge; the "or say raid needs a forge" branch is excluded).
- [ ] 11. Hunt's fast tier before the merge request includes `make lint` (ruff), so a lint failure is caught before review (raid 2026-10-27: #1733 lost a gate round to ruff E731).
- [ ] 8. Hunt's `TMPDIR="$W/.tmp"` advice makes `tests/test_harness_doctor_skill.py::test_refusal_ignores_an_exported_work_tree` and `::test_refusal_outside_harness[no-repo]` fail (reproduced 2026-10-27: fail with TMPDIR in the worktree, pass with the default); fix the tests or the advice.
- [ ] 9. Gaze takes only a PR number: no route for forge-less projects, and launched from a session whose cwd is another repo it resolves the wrong forge. Give it a branch/repo argument or document the limit.
- [ ] 10. (low) The self-gate runs before the rebase, as before 1235; decide whether to swap.
- [ ] 12. Gaze says when it ran alone: when no seat other than the caller could run (e.g. a nesting limit), the result carries that fact in its output shape (`seats: self-only`) instead of a plain REVIEWED, and the reuse rule (`skills/merge/SKILL.md` § Gating tiers and raid Phase 6) treats a self-only record as missing. Hunt is not changed to behave differently in a raid; the fix is gaze's honesty plus the reuse rule.
- [ ] 13. Claude Code subagent nesting depth: set `CLAUDE_CODE_MAX_SUBAGENT_SPAWN_DEPTH` to at least 2 in `settings.shared.json`'s `env` (projected into ~/.claude/settings.json by `idh install`) so a raid's coder can run gaze with real seats, consistent with `rules/claude-code.md` § Subagent levers; Codex and Pi need their own equivalent or fall back to item 12. Never edit ~/.claude/settings.json directly.

## Relevant files
- `skills/hunt/SKILL.md`
- `skills/raid/SKILL.md`
- `skills/gaze/SKILL.md`
- `rules/workflow.md`
- `tests/test_harness_doctor_skill.py`

## Test
Wording items take no tests. Item 8 is a test fix; item 2's helper, if built, gets tests.

## Raid annotation (Imagine+Plan, 2026-10-27)
Checked against main f52b159e (post #1733/#1735/#1736/#1738).
- 1 valid: hunt Plan has no surprise rule (only "Judgment needed" bullets). Add one bullet to Plan, pointing at workflow.md § Escalation protocol. skills/hunt.
- 2 valid: nothing in Plan reads open MRs or locked worktrees. Simplest: one Plan sentence naming the two reads (`git worktree list` for locked trees, forge MR list with files, or none without a forge), then name/coordinate/escalate at 3+. No helper script (answer to "decide": no; two commands, no logic). skills/hunt.
- 3 valid: hunt Execute says only "goes back up as in Plan"; raid Phase 5 says "schedule the children in a later wave", silent on the locked worktree, partial branch, and no later wave. Add one sentence each: unlock+keep branch pushed/noted in the split, and "no later wave left: report the split to the author". skills/hunt, skills/raid.
- 4 valid: workflow.md:135-140 gives orchestrator/hunt/interactive, no lone autonomous session. Add ~60 chars: "A lone autonomous session proposes it in its report and stops." workflow.md.
- 5 valid: Detach "a returned monster included", Plan "Too big or multipart" (long), Execute "goes back up" and raid 244-246 all restate it. Cut Execute clause and shorten Plan bullet to a pointer. Net shrink. skills/hunt.
- 6 valid: hunt Verify "stage `tickets/`" still wholesale; merge/SKILL.md:89 has the narrow form. Copy it. skills/hunt.
- 7 valid: raid Phase 6 (`gaze <pr>`, forge wording) and Phase 7 assume a PR. Simplest honest action: one line "raid needs a forge; a forge-less ready branch goes to the author with the hunt report". Cheaper than a new path. skills/raid.
- 8 valid, reproduced: with TMPDIR inside the worktree, `test_refusal_outside_harness[no-repo]` fails (rc 0). Cause (isolated): pytest tmp_path then sits inside the harness checkout, so the "no repo" cwd resolves to the harness; harness_here.sh is correct. Fix the tests: build the foreign cwd outside REPO (mkdtemp under /tmp, or skip when tmp_path is under REPO). Keep hunt's advice. tests/test_harness_doctor_skill.py. The ticket's second name (exported_work_tree) passed in my run with TMPDIR set; only no-repo failed, so re-measure before editing.
- 9 valid: gaze Input is PR-number only; "no PR argument" -> ESCALATE. Simplest: document the limit (forge-less projects use hunt's reviewer seats; run from the PR's repo cwd). Adding a repo argument is a feature. skills/gaze.
- 10 valid, low: hunt Verify runs self-gate then rebase. Swap = rebase first (rules/git.md "Rebase before every gate"). One-line reorder; do it.

Monster check: one sign-off unit (wording of 5 files, one test fix, ~5 files, no dependents, no build gate). Items 1-2 are decided in session. Verdict GO as one PR; no split.
Resident budget: rules/*.md resident total 17517 chars vs RESIDENT_BUDGET 17800 (tests/test_rules_resident_budget.py:56): 283 headroom. Item 4's ~60 chars fits; do not raise the budget.
Tests: first failing = tests/test_harness_doctor_skill.py::test_refusal_outside_harness[no-repo] under TMPDIR=<worktree>/.tmp (red before, green after; run both with and without TMPDIR). Wording items take no tests; resist pinning hunt text. Tautology check: a test that only passes because tmp_path is outside the repo proves nothing, so the fixed test must assert rc 1 from a cwd verified to be outside REPO.
Conflicts: 1247 touches only the top IDH_ROOT paragraph of every skill (disjoint hunks). 1248 touches gaze_close/gaze_setup plus one raid marker line (item 9 edits gaze Input prose, item 7 raid Phase 6-7; rebase, no overlap expected). 1244 touches merge skill and tickets only. Rebase after those land.
